  "title": "Te Puea Hērangi",
  "summary": "A Tainui leader who became established during the First World War through her campaign against conscription of the Tainui. In 1921 she bought the land at Ngāruawāhia on which Tūrangawaewae marae was built, now the headquarters of the Kīngitanga (Māori King Movement); its meeting house Māhinaarangi dates from 1929. She was born in 1883 and died in 1952.",
